---
layout: changelog
title: "Deploy Sites and Functions from Entire repositories"
date: 2026-10-27
cover: /images/blog/announcing-appwrite-entire-partnership/cover.avif
tags: sites, functions, integrations
---

Appwrite is partnering with [Entire](https://entire.io), the Git forge for agents, and Entire now joins Appwrite's Git providers. Connect an Entire project from **Project settings** > **Git configuration**, approve the installation on entire.io, and [deploy from Git](/docs/products/sites/deploy-from-git) on every push.

Pushes to your production branch build and activate. Pushes to other branches build without activating, and Sites get a private [preview link](/docs/products/sites/previews). Unless Silent mode is on, each build reports back to the commit on Entire as a check run. Entire is available as a Git provider on Appwrite Cloud.

